    "pageTitle": "Concrete Patios",
    "seoTitle": "Concrete Patio Contractor in Dunwoody, GA",
    "metaDescription": "Build a durable backyard concrete patio in Dunwoody, GA. Brook Concrete Company installs plain, colored and stamped patios. Request a free estimate.",
    "urlSlug": "/concrete-patios/",
    "htmlContent": "<h1>Concrete Patio Contractor in Dunwoody, GA</h1>\n<p>A beautifully designed and professionally installed concrete patio is the cornerstone of comfortable outdoor living. At Brook Concrete Company, we are Dunwoody's leading concrete patio contractor, helping homeowners turn underutilized backyard spaces into elegant, functional outdoor retreats. Whether you envision a sleek modern patio for quiet evening relaxation, a sprawling entertainment deck for neighborhood barbecues, or a multi-tiered hardscape complete with fire pit seating, our skilled team delivers exceptional results tailored to your lifestyle and budget.</p>\n<p>Concrete is widely recognized as the premier material for outdoor patios due to its unmatched versatility, superior longevity, and low maintenance requirements. Unlike wooden decks that warp, splinter, and require annual staining, or individual pavers that shift and allow weeds to sprout, poured concrete provides a continuous, durable surface built to endure Georgia's humid summers and rainy winters with effortless grace. For elevated elegance, many homeowners upgrade to <a href=\"/stamped-concrete/\">stamped concrete</a> for distinct texture and natural appeal.</p>\n<h2>Custom Patio Design and Installation in Dunwoody</h2>\n<p>Every backyard in Dunwoody is unique, characterized by varying slope contours, shade conditions, and architectural styles. Our patio installation process begins with an in-depth design consultation. We examine how rainwater flows across your yard, ensuring that your new patio is engineered with a gentle slope that directs water away from your home's foundation.</p>\n<p>We handle all excavation and site preparation, clearing organic turf and stabilizing native clay soils with a compacted crushed gravel sub-base. We build custom forms to achieve your desired layout—whether clean geometric rectangles, gentle flowing curves, or multi-level platforms that step down gracefully into your garden. Every patio slab is poured with high-strength concrete and reinforced with welded wire mesh or structural rebar to ensure long-term structural integrity.</p>\n<h2>Explore Diverse Finishes and Decorative Textures</h2>\n<p>At Brook Concrete Company, we believe that an outdoor patio should reflect your personal aesthetic. We offer a rich variety of finishes and architectural touches, including our premium <a href=\"/decorative-concrete/\">decorative concrete</a> options:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Non-Slip Broom Finish:</strong> A classic, clean brushed surface that provides reliable traction underfoot, even when wet.</li>\n<li><strong>Smooth Hand-Troweled Borders:</strong> Framing a brushed field with polished, smooth margins for a sophisticated, contemporary look.</li>\n<li><strong>Exposed Aggregate:</strong> Revealing natural rounded river stones or colored pebbles for an organic, textured surface with superior durability.</li>\n<li><strong>Integral and Acid-Stained Colors:</strong> Infusing your concrete with warm earth tones, terra cottas, or rich charcoals that coordinate seamlessly with your home's exterior palette.</li>\n<li><strong>Stamped Patterns:</strong> Replicating high-end natural stone materials like flagstone, slate, cobblestone, or fieldstone without masonry price tags.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Built for Grills, Fire Pits, and Outdoor Kitchens</h2>\n<p>Modern backyard living often includes heavy amenities such as built-in gas grills, stone fire pits, outdoor pizza ovens, heavy pergolas, and hot tubs. When installing your patio, we account for these future additions by pouring thicker reinforced pads in dedicated zones to safely support substantial concentrated loads without risk of settlement cracking. Furthermore, connecting your patio to the front driveway or garden with a matching <a href=\"/concrete-walkways/\">concrete walkway</a> creates an integrated, accessible outdoor environment.</p>\n<h2>Strategic Control Joints for Crack Prevention</h2>\n<p>All concrete naturally shrinks as it cures. The mark of an expert contractor is knowing how to control that shrinkage. We place saw-cut or hand-tooled control joints at precise intervals, creating planned stress-relief lines that guide microscopic shrinkage fractures beneath the surface where they remain invisible. Our methods strictly adhere to quality standards promoted by the <a href=\"https://www.cement.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Portland Cement Association</a>.</p>\n<h2>Our Step-by-Step Patio Construction Workflow</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>On-Site Consultation:</strong> We review your ideas, measure the area, evaluate yard elevations, and provide a clear written estimate.</li>\n<li><strong>Excavation &amp; Sub-Base Preparation:</strong> We remove turf, grade the soil, and compact a dense stone base to prevent settlement.</li>\n<li><strong>Formwork &amp; Reinforcement:</strong> We construct precision timber forms and install reinforcing steel elevated above the gravel bed.</li>\n<li><strong>Pouring &amp; Surface Finishing:</strong> We pour high-quality concrete, screed it smooth, and apply your chosen decorative texture or finish.</li>\n<li><strong>Curing &amp; Job Site Cleanup:</strong> We protect the curing slab, remove all construction forms, clean your yard thoroughly, and conduct a final walkthrough.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3>How thick should a residential concrete patio be?</h3>\n<p>Standard residential concrete patios are poured 4 inches thick. For areas designed to support heavy amenities like outdoor fireplaces, masonry kitchens, or hot tubs, we pour 6 inches with heavy rebar reinforcement.</p>\n<h3>Can a new concrete patio be added onto an existing slab?</h3>\n<p>Yes. We can expand existing patios by installing expansion joints and drilling steel dowels into the existing concrete to securely tie the sections together while allowing necessary thermal movement.</p>\n<h2>Request Your Free Patio Estimate in Dunwoody</h2>\n<p>Ready to build the backyard patio of your dreams? Contact Brook Concrete Company today to schedule your free consultation and estimate in Dunwoody, GA!</p>",
