    "pageTitle": "Concrete Steps",
    "seoTitle": "Concrete Steps Contractor in Dunwoody, GA",
    "metaDescription": "Brook Concrete Company builds and replaces concrete front steps, stairs and landings in Dunwoody, GA. Safe, sturdy and built to code.",
    "urlSlug": "/concrete-steps/",
    "htmlContent": "<h1>Concrete Steps Contractor in Dunwoody, GA</h1>\n<p>Entryway steps are one of the most vital architectural features of any home or commercial building. They provide essential vertical access between elevation changes, safeguard occupants against trip-and-fall hazards, and contribute significantly to overall exterior curb appeal. At Brook Concrete Company, we are Dunwoody's trusted concrete steps contractor, specializing in the design, pouring, replacement, and repair of custom concrete stairs, porch landings, and terraced landscape steps.</p>\n<p>In north Georgia's undulating topography, sloped lots and multi-level home designs frequently require sturdy exterior steps. Wooden stairs warp, rot, and harbor termites, while poorly constructed masonry units loosen and shift. Poured monolithic concrete steps provide an unyielding, permanent structure capable of enduring heavy foot traffic, severe weather, and decades of relentless use without wobbling or degradation. Pairing custom steps with an elegant new <a href=\"/concrete-walkways/\">concrete walkway</a> creates a cohesive, welcoming entrance.</p>\n<h2>Residential Entry Steps and Front Porch Landings</h2>\n<p>A crumbling, tilted, or uneven front staircase detracts from your home's appearance and poses severe safety risks for family, guests, and delivery couriers. Brook Concrete Company constructs custom front entry stairs and expansive porch landings tailored to your home's exterior proportions. We adhere strictly to residential building codes, guaranteeing uniform riser heights (typically 7 to 7.5 inches) and tread depths (11 to 12 inches) so climbing feels natural, comfortable, and intuitive.</p>\n<p>We build our steps with a subtle 1/4-inch forward pitch per foot on every tread, ensuring rainwater sheds immediately off the nose rather than pooling on surfaces where it could freeze or create slippery algae patches.</p>\n<h2>Commercial Concrete Stairs and Code Compliance</h2>\n<p>Commercial facilities, retail centers, apartment complexes, and office buildings in Dunwoody require high-capacity concrete stairs that comply with stringent International Building Code (IBC) and ADA guidelines. We construct heavy-duty commercial stairwells featuring precision handrail block-outs, non-skid nosing textures, and integrated landings. Our commercial pours use high-compressive-strength mixes reinforced with heavy steel rebar to safely manage continuous daily foot traffic.</p>\n<h2>Replacing Damaged, Tilting, or Separating Steps</h2>\n<p>One of the most common issues Dunwoody homeowners face is front porch steps pulling away from the foundation. This dangerous separation occurs when previous contractors poured heavy concrete over uncompacted backfill soil without doweling into the home's foundation wall. Over time, the soil settles, causing the entire staircase to tilt forward or sink into the ground.</p>\n<p>When steps have structurally detached or sustained deep internal fractures, complete replacement is the only responsible fix. Our crew safely breaks out and removes the failing stairs, excavates down to stable subsoil, pours reinforced structural footings, and mechanically anchors new steps directly into your foundation with heavy steel rebar pins. However, if your steps are structurally sound and merely suffer from surface pitting or minor cosmetic chips, specialized <a href=\"/concrete-resurfacing/\">concrete resurfacing</a> can restore a pristine appearance at a fraction of replacement costs.</p>\n<h2>Decorative Finishes, Colors, and Railing Integration</h2>\n<p>Your exterior steps can be customized with a variety of architectural finishes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Non-Slip Broom Finish:</strong> The industry standard for outdoor stair treads, providing dependable traction during rainy Georgia weather.</li>\n<li><strong>Smooth-Troweled Risers with Textured Treads:</strong> A sleek modern contrast featuring crisp polished vertical faces framed against slip-resistant steps.</li>\n<li><strong>Stamped and Colored Finishes:</strong> Imprinting slate or stone patterns to coordinate with your front porch, walkway, or backyard <a href=\"/concrete-patios/\">concrete patios</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Core-Drilled Railing Pockets:</strong> We coordinate with wrought iron and aluminum railing fabricators to install secure anchor sleeves directly into the concrete.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Our Engineering Standards and Precision Craftsmanship</h2>\n<p>Building concrete stairs requires meticulous carpenter craftsmanship to construct rigid, watertight forms that resist hydraulic concrete pressure during placement. We vibrate freshly placed concrete to eliminate unsightly honeycomb voids along riser faces, resulting in smooth, dense, durable vertical surfaces. Our engineering methods strictly comply with standards established by the <a href=\"https://www.concrete.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">American Concrete Institute</a>.</p>\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3>Can settled concrete steps simply be mudjacked or lifted?</h3>\n<p>While foam lifting or mudjacking can sometimes temporarily raise small slabs, heavy multi-step concrete units often exceed lifting capacity or crack further during injection. Poured structural replacement provides an unyielding, permanent foundation that will not sink again.</p>\n<h3>How soon can we use our new concrete steps after pouring?</h3>\n<p>Light foot traffic is generally permissible after 24 to 48 hours, though we recommend using an alternate entrance for 48 hours to allow the concrete nose and edges to cure without disturbance.</p>\n<h2>Request Your Free Concrete Steps Estimate</h2>\n<p>Ensure your home or business entrances are safe, attractive, and built to last. Contact Brook Concrete Company today to schedule your complimentary concrete steps consultation and estimate in Dunwoody, GA!</p>",
