    "pageTitle": "Driveway Replacement",
    "seoTitle": "Concrete Driveway Replacement Dunwoody, GA",
    "metaDescription": "Cracked or sunken driveway? Brook Concrete Company handles concrete driveway replacement in Dunwoody, GA with proper base prep. Free estimates.",
    "urlSlug": "/concrete-driveway-replacement/",
    "htmlContent": "<h1>Concrete Driveway Replacement in Dunwoody, GA</h1>\n<p>Is your home's driveway covered in unsightly cracks, sunken slabs, or crumbling surfaces? An aged, failing driveway not only detracts from your property's curb appeal but also poses severe trip hazards and risks vehicle tire damage. At Brook Concrete Company, we specialize in comprehensive concrete driveway replacement throughout Dunwoody, GA, and surrounding north metro Atlanta communities. We handle every phase of the replacement process—from complete demolition and environmentally responsible debris hauling to subgrade soil stabilization, laser-leveled formwork, and precision pouring.</p>\n<p>If you are exploring your options, start by reviewing our comprehensive <a href=\"/concrete-driveways/\">concrete driveways</a> overview. Our goal is to provide you with a brand-new driveway built to endure decades of heavy vehicle use and regional weather extremes without settling or premature failure.</p>\n<h2>Recognizing the Signs That Your Driveway Needs Full Replacement</h2>\n<p>While minor cosmetic blemishes can often be patched, certain structural defects indicate that your existing driveway has reached the end of its useful lifespan. Key signs that call for complete replacement include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Alligator or Web Cracking:</strong> Interconnected, spiderweb-like fractures across multiple slabs indicate that the underlying soil has settled or washed out.</li>\n<li><strong>Severe Sunken or Heaved Slabs:</strong> Sections that have shifted several inches out of alignment create dangerous trip hazards and cause water to pool toward your garage or foundation.</li>\n<li><strong>Deep Surface Spalling and Delamination:</strong> Flaking, pitted concrete where aggregate stones are completely exposed cannot be permanently repaired with surface patches.</li>\n<li><strong>Recurring Drainage and Ponding Issues:</strong> Standing water that remains on your driveway hours after rainfall accelerates sub-base erosion and degrades the slab.</li>\n<li><strong>Driveway Age Exceeding 25–30 Years:</strong> Concrete naturally degrades over time due to repeated thermal expansion, water penetration, and vehicle loading.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Our Demolition and Base Rebuilding Process</h2>\n<p>The secret to an enduring driveway replacement lies in what happens after the old slab is broken up. Many cut-rate contractors simply pour new concrete over old, degraded gravel. At Brook Concrete Company, our crew utilizes specialized hydraulic breakers and mini-excavators to cleanly remove your failed driveway. We haul the old concrete to certified recycling facilities where it is crushed into reusable aggregate.</p>\n<p>Once the subgrade is exposed, we evaluate Georgia's native red clay soil. We excavate soft, organic soil pockets and install a heavy layer of crushed granite GAB (Graded Aggregate Base). We use mechanical plate compactors to consolidate this stone base into a solid foundation that prevents future shifting, washouts, and settling.</p>\n<h2>Replacement vs. Resurfacing: Choosing the Right Solution</h2>\n<p>Property owners frequently ask whether resurfacing is an alternative to full demolition. If your driveway is structurally intact with sound soil support and only minor cosmetic weathering, <a href=\"/concrete-resurfacing/\">concrete resurfacing</a> can be a viable, budget-conscious choice. However, if the subgrade has collapsed or slabs have cracked completely through, applying a thin overlay is a waste of money—cracks will quickly telegraph right through the new surface. During our free on-site consultation, we provide an honest assessment so you invest in the right long-term solution.</p>\n<h2>Upgrade Your Home's Aesthetic with Custom Features</h2>\n<p>A driveway replacement is the ideal opportunity to redesign and enhance your home's front exterior. You are not locked into the exact footprint of your old driveway. During replacement, we can widen narrow sections for easier two-car parking, add turnarounds, incorporate elegant curves, or build a matching <a href=\"/concrete-walkways/\">concrete walkway</a> connecting your driveway directly to your front porch or side yard. We also offer decorative finishes such as stamped borders, colored concrete aprons, and picture-framed smooth borders around brushed fields.</p>\n<h2>Our Step-by-Step Replacement Workflow</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Detailed Consultation &amp; Plan:</strong> We measure your driveway, evaluate drainage pitch, confirm property boundaries, and outline design options.</li>\n<li><strong>Demolition &amp; Removal:</strong> We break up old concrete, protect surrounding sod and irrigation lines, and haul away all debris.</li>\n<li><strong>Sub-Base Compaction:</strong> We install and mechanically compact a thick crushed gravel base to establish an unwavering foundation.</li>\n<li><strong>Forming &amp; Reinforcement:</strong> We construct heavy-duty forms and install steel rebar grids elevated on chairs for internal tensile strength.</li>\n<li><strong>Pouring &amp; Finishing:</strong> We pour high-strength ready-mix concrete, screed, float, edge, and apply a non-slip broom finish.</li>\n<li><strong>Joint Cutting &amp; Curing:</strong> We cut precision contraction joints and apply curing compound, following guidance from the <a href=\"https://www.concrete.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">American Concrete Institute</a>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3>How long does concrete driveway replacement take?</h3>\n<p>A typical residential replacement takes two to three days: one day for demolition and base prep, and one to two days for forming, pouring, and finishing. Curing requires 7 days before passenger vehicles can drive on the new surface.</p>\n<h3>Will demolition damage my lawn or landscaping?</h3>\n<p>Our crews use specialized turf-friendly equipment and lay down protective plywood mats where necessary to protect your grass, flower beds, and irrigation heads.</p>\n<h2>Schedule Your Dunwoody Driveway Replacement Today</h2>\n<p>Say goodbye to cracked, crumbling concrete. Contact Brook Concrete Company today to schedule your complimentary on-site inspection and free replacement estimate!</p>",
