    "pageTitle": "Concrete Slabs",
    "seoTitle": "Concrete Slab Contractor in Dunwoody, GA",
    "metaDescription": "Brook Concrete Company installs concrete slabs for garages, sheds, workshops and additions in Dunwoody, GA. Level, strong and built right.",
    "urlSlug": "/concrete-slabs/",
    "htmlContent": "<h1>Concrete Slab Contractor in Dunwoody, GA</h1>\n<p>A properly engineered and poured concrete slab provides the indispensable structural foundation for countless residential and commercial applications. Whether you are building a detached two-car garage, erecting a backyard storage shed, setting up a heavy-duty workshop, installing a swim spa, or placing heavy commercial mechanical equipment, the performance of the entire structure relies on the integrity of the slab beneath it. At Brook Concrete Company, we are Dunwoody's trusted concrete slab contractor, providing precision-graded, level, and heavily reinforced concrete slabs engineered to support substantial loads for decades without settling or cracking.</p>\n<p>For load-bearing building additions and complete structures requiring deep perimeter footings, explore our comprehensive <a href=\"/concrete-foundations/\">concrete foundations</a> capabilities. For standalone pads and flatwork, our team brings decades of combined expertise, top-grade ready-mix formulations, and laser-accurate leveling to every project across Dunwoody and north metro Atlanta.</p>\n<h2>Slabs for Garages, Storage Sheds, and Workshops</h2>\n<p>Accessory outbuildings require stable, moisture-controlled concrete floors. Erecting a prefabricated garage or custom timber shed over bare dirt, unlevel gravel, or timber framing leaves your building vulnerable to rot, rodent intrusion, and structural shifting. We pour monolithic floating slabs and turned-down edge slabs tailored to your building kit's exact footprint.</p>\n<p>Our garage and shed slabs feature a compacted gravel sub-base, heavy vapor barriers to prevent ground humidity from rusting tools and equipment, and perimeter-thickened footings that safely distribute wall loads into the ground. We finish the surface with a hard-troweled smooth finish that is easy to sweep, seal, or coat with epoxy.</p>\n<h2>Equipment Pads and Heavy Utility Slabs</h2>\n<p>Modern homes and commercial facilities depend on heavy, vibration-generating equipment that requires a solid, perfectly level mounting surface. Brook Concrete Company pours custom utility slabs for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Whole-house backup generators that require vibration-isolated pads</li>\n<li>Commercial and residential HVAC condenser units</li>\n<li>Backyard hot tubs and heavy swim spas that exert thousands of pounds of hydrostatic pressure</li>\n<li>Pool filtration equipment and automated water pump skids</li>\n<li>Trash dumpster enclosures and commercial waste compactors</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Determining the Proper Slab Thickness and Reinforcement</h2>\n<p>A primary cause of slab failure is inadequate thickness. While standard light-duty walkways are poured 4 inches thick, heavy vehicle garages and equipment slabs often require 5 to 6 inches or more of high-strength concrete. Learn more in our detailed educational guide on <a href=\"/blog/concrete-slab-thickness/\">how thick a concrete slab should be</a>.</p>\n<p>Furthermore, internal reinforcement is non-negotiable for structural slabs. We install tied steel rebar grids (typically #4 rebar on 12-to-18-inch centers) elevated on plastic chairs so the steel is positioned securely in the middle third of the slab, providing maximum flexural strength against vehicle point loads. Smooth transitions from your garage slab to outdoor <a href=\"/concrete-driveways/\">concrete driveways</a> ensure seamless access for all vehicles.</p>\n<h2>Vapor Barriers and Subgrade Compaction</h2>\n<p>In north Georgia, groundwater moisture constantly evaporates upward through permeable soil. When pouring interior slabs for enclosed garages or workshops, we install heavy-duty 10-mil to 15-mil poly vapor retarders directly underneath the concrete. This barrier halts capillary moisture transmission, preventing damp concrete floors, peeling epoxy coatings, and musty mildew odors.</p>\n<p>Beneath the vapor barrier, we install a clean, compacted crushed granite aggregate base (GAB). Proper mechanical compaction with vibrating plate tampers eliminates air pockets and prevents post-pour soil settlement, adhering to guidelines published by the <a href=\"https://www.cement.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Portland Cement Association</a>.</p>\n<h2>Our Step-by-Step Concrete Slab Construction Workflow</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Site Assessment &amp; Laser Leveling:</strong> We review equipment specifications, shoot elevation benchmarks with laser levels, and mark the footprint.</li>\n<li><strong>Excavation &amp; Sub-Base Compaction:</strong> We excavate unsuitable topsoil and compact a dense crushed gravel stone base.</li>\n<li><strong>Formwork &amp; Perimeter Trenching:</strong> We erect rigid dimensional lumber forms, trench thickened edges where necessary, and install vapor retarders.</li>\n<li><strong>Rebar Grid Installation:</strong> We assemble tied steel rebar grids elevated on chairs to guarantee internal structural tensile capacity.</li>\n<li><strong>Concrete Placement &amp; Screeding:</strong> We pour 3,500 to 4,000+ PSI concrete, screed it flat with power screeds, and consolidate the mix with mechanical vibrators.</li>\n<li><strong>Floating, Finishing &amp; Saw-Cutting:</strong> We power-trowel the surface to your specified finish and saw-cut contraction joints to manage thermal stresses.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3>How long must I wait before building on my new concrete slab?</h3>\n<p>Concrete reaches roughly 70% of its design strength within 7 days. Most carpenters and building erectors can frame walls after 7 days, with full curing reached at 28 days.</p>\n<h3>Do I need anchor bolts embedded in the slab for framing?</h3>\n<p>Yes. If you provide your building plans, our crew will embed code-compliant galvanized J-bolts or mudsill anchors directly into the perimeter concrete while it is still plastic.</p>\n<h2>Get a Free Estimate on Your Concrete Slab</h2>\n<p>Ensure your upcoming building or equipment is supported by a flawless concrete slab. Contact Brook Concrete Company today to schedule your complimentary site consultation and written estimate in Dunwoody, GA!</p>",
