    "pageTitle": "Concrete Pool Decks",
    "seoTitle": "Concrete Pool Deck Contractor Dunwoody, GA",
    "metaDescription": "Brook Concrete Company installs concrete pool decks in Dunwoody, GA with slip-resistant, cool-to-touch finishes. Request a free estimate.",
    "urlSlug": "/concrete-pool-decks/",
    "htmlContent": "<h1>Concrete Pool Deck Contractor Dunwoody, GA</h1>\n<p>An inground swimming pool is the centerpiece of summer outdoor living and entertainment in Dunwoody, GA. However, the true beauty, comfort, and safety of your pool area depend largely on the quality of the surrounding pool deck. At Brook Concrete Company, we are Dunwoody's trusted concrete pool deck contractor, specializing in the installation, replacement, and resurfacing of custom concrete pool surrounds. We build decks that seamlessly combine slip resistance, cool-to-the-touch surfaces, and breathtaking architectural elegance.</p>\n<p>Concrete is widely recognized as the premier material for pool decking because it provides a continuous, durable surface that withstands splashing chlorinated water, chemical pool treatments, and intense Georgia sunshine. Whether you are building a new pool or replacing an aged, cracked deck, our team delivers custom flatwork tailored to your leisure lifestyle. For luxury aesthetics, many clients choose our custom <a href=\"/stamped-concrete/\">stamped concrete</a> finishes that replicate natural quarried stone.</p>\n<h2>Slip-Resistant Textures Engineered for Family Safety</h2>\n<p>Safety is the paramount priority around any swimming pool. Wet concrete can become slick if finished improperly, creating dangerous slip-and-fall hazards for running children and visiting guests. At Brook Concrete Company, we specialize in high-traction, non-slip finishes specifically engineered for wet environments:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Light Broom and Swirl Textures:</strong> Subtle directional brushing that provides dependable traction underfoot while remaining smooth enough for bare feet.</li>\n<li><strong>Textured Decorative Stamping:</strong> Imprinting subtle natural slate or stone textures that provide natural traction crevices without sharp edges.</li>\n<li><strong>Exposed Aggregate Surrounds:</strong> Washing away surface cement paste to reveal rounded river pebbles that provide outstanding natural slip resistance.</li>\n<li><strong>Polymer Anti-Slip Additives:</strong> Blending microscopic polymer aggregate granules into protective clear sealers to create an invisible, barefoot-friendly gripping texture.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Cool-Touch Deck Finishes for Blistering Summer Heat</h2>\n<p>During the height of Georgia summers, unshaded pool decks can absorb intense solar radiation, heating up to temperatures that burn bare feet. Brook Concrete Company offers specialized cool deck solutions that dramatically reduce surface heat absorption. By utilizing light-reflective color hardeners, pastel integral color tones, and specialized micro-topping overlays, we keep your pool deck comfortable and inviting to walk on even during the hottest July afternoons.</p>\n<h2>Drainage, Slope Pitch, and Coping Integration</h2>\n<p>Proper water management is essential for long-term pool deck performance. An improperly graded pool deck allows splashed pool water, dirty landscape runoff, and torrential stormwater to drain back into the clean pool water or pond against your home's foundation. We pour every pool deck with a precise laser-guided slope (typically 1/4 inch per foot) directing runoff away from the coping edge into deck drains or surrounding landscape beds.</p>\n<p>We also coordinate precision cantilevers or bullnose coping forms around the pool lip, creating seamless transitions between the swimming pool coping and the broad lounging deck.</p>\n<h2>Pool Deck Replacement and Structural Restoration</h2>\n<p>Over time, chlorinated water penetration, shifting backfill soils, and plumbing leak settlements can cause older pool decks to tilt, crack, and separate from pool coping tiles. Settled slabs create dangerous stubbed-toe hazards and allow water to erode soil behind pool walls. When damage is isolated, our <a href=\"/concrete-repair/\">concrete repair</a> team can inject flexible joint sealants and level uneven slabs. For decks with extensive cracking, complete replacement provides a stunning, durable reset.</p>\n<p>A new pool deck also pairs naturally with an adjacent <a href=\"/concrete-patios/\">concrete patio</a> to create an expansive, unified backyard entertainment environment. All our structural pool flatwork adheres to standards published by the <a href=\"https://www.concrete.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">American Concrete Institute</a>.</p>\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3>Can you pour a new concrete pool deck around an existing swimming pool?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Our crews take extensive precautions to protect your pool plaster, fiberglass shell, coping stones, and filtration equipment during demolition and pouring, ensuring zero debris enters your pool.</p>\n<h3>How do you control cracking around curved pool shapes?</h3>\n<p>We install flexible expansion joint material around the pool perimeter and saw-cut radial control joints extending outward from coping edges to accommodate natural thermal movement.</p>\n<h2>Schedule Your Dunwoody Pool Deck Consultation</h2>\n<p>Transform your backyard pool into a luxurious, safe outdoor oasis. Contact Brook Concrete Company today to schedule your complimentary pool deck consultation and written estimate in Dunwoody, GA!</p>",
